From 92c1ada97636ca6f462890a43c0cdd72b02b5f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:34:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 117/117] scripting: a shader constant's script has the
 effect's material as thisObject
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A script on an effect's shader constant (constantshadervalues: {"value", "script"}) ran with thisObject =
the layer. In WE it is not the layer: 3163060610's cloud layer (`主要云`, 1743 x 1508) carries a
waterripple whose `scale` constant's script does `thisObject.scale = c_de_scale + 0.1` (0.22), and WE
draws the cloud whole across the window; LWE scaled the layer to 0.22 (health bbox 383 x 332) and the
cloud was gone. Every constant script in the library (32, in 3163060610 and 2890767643) sets
`thisObject.<its own constant>` — the effect's material properties by their material names.

thisObject is now a material object: an accessor per constant of the effect (its constantshadervalues
keys; get / set the constant in every pass that has it, live), and getAnimation () bound to the layer
as before (the running constant's own keyframe animation). thisLayer is still the layer.

3163060610 against WE: 0.119 → 0.059 (2 s 0.082 → 0.002, 5 s 0.084 → 0.002).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md 3163060610 (the big cloud missing)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
